From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the TCL Book 14 Go

Add the TCL Book 14 Go (B220G), a 14" Snapdragon 7c laptop with a
1366x768 panel and LTE. It builds on sc7180-cls07180-ufs.dtsi and adds
what its DSDT puts on i2c4 (QUP0 SE4, I2C5 in ACPI).

- The keyboard (QTEC0001) is a HID device at 0x05 with its interrupt
  on GPIO 33, active low with a pull-up, and its _DSM puts the HID
  descriptor at 0x20.
- The touchpad (QTEC0002) is at 0x2c with its interrupt on GPIO 94, and
  its _DSM also puts the descriptor at 0x20. The PEP drives GPIO 25 high
  for it in D0, so that GPIO enables its supply, as on the Aspire 1.

Left out:

- The panel sits behind a DSI to eDP bridge (EDPBridge) at 0x29 on
  i2c10, with GPIOs 13, 20, 21, 23, 26 and 51. The Aspire 1's SN65DSI86
  answers at 0x2c or 0x2d, so this is another chip, and the DSDT reads
  the panel description from firmware memory at boot. Neither the bridge
  nor the panel can be named, so the panel stays on the firmware's
  framebuffer, without brightness control.
- An Awinic SAR sensor (AWDZ9610X) at 0x12 on i2c4, interrupt on
  GPIO 34, whose exact part the DSDT doesn't give.
- The battery, charger and lid, which the EC reports.

The "tcl" vendor prefix is Toby Churchill Ltd.'s, so the compatible
uses "tclcomm", after the SMBIOS maker TCL Communication Ltd.

No Windows Update bundle answers the laptop's IDs, so its firmware has
to come from an owner's Windows install. The modem image is the
WLAN-only qcmpss7180_nm.mbn, which the LIVA and Aspire 1 load as well,
since the full LTE image (62 MB on the Lenovo 10w) doesn't fit
the 32 MiB modem carve-out these firmwares share. Not booted on the
laptop yet.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-tcl-book-14-go.dts   | 99 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 99 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-tcl-book-14-go.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-tcl-book-14-go.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-tcl-book-14-go.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fb8067f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-tcl-book-14-go.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * TCL Book 14 Go (B220G)
+ *
+ * Its DSDT puts the keyboard (QTEC0001) and touchpad (QTEC0002) on i2c4
+ * and the panel behind a DSI to eDP bridge at 0x29 on i2c10 (EDPBridge),
+ * whose chip it doesn't name. The panel stays on the firmware's
+ * framebuffer, so the display subsystem and GPU stay off.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "sc7180-cls07180-ufs.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	model = "TCL Book 14 Go";
+	compatible = "tclcomm,book-14-go", "qcom,sc7180";
+	chassis-type = "laptop";
+
+	reg_tp_vdd: touchpad-regulator {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "tp_vdd";
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 25 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&reg_tp_en_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c4 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	keyboard@5 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x05>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 33 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&hid_keyboard_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+
+	touchpad@2c {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x2c>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		vdd-supply = <&reg_tp_vdd>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 94 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&hid_touchpad_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/tcl/book-14-go/qcadsp7180.mbn";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_mpss {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/tcl/book-14-go/qcmpss7180_nm.mbn";
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	hid_keyboard_default: hid-keyboard-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio33";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	hid_touchpad_default: hid-touchpad-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio94";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	reg_tp_en_default: reg-tp-en-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio25";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+
+&venus {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/tcl/book-14-go/qcvss7180.mbn";
+};
